@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy & Zero-Telemetry Transparency — SaveZonix";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <partial name="_LegalNav" model='(string)"Privacy"' />

        <div class="legal-header">
            <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy &amp; Zero-Telemetry Notice</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>Effective Date: January 1, 2026</span>
                <span>Last Updated: October 19, 2026</span>
                <span>GDPR &bull; CCPA Compliant &bull; Zero-Telemetry Standards</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>PRIVACY FIRST ARCHITECTURE:</strong> SaveZonix is an independent media analysis and stream utility engineered on a strict zero-telemetry and local-execution privacy model. We do not sell, rent, or monetize your personal information. We do not track the URLs you analyze, deploy third-party advertising tracking scripts, or build behavioral user profiles.
            </div>

            <h2>1. Client-Side Processing &amp; Zero Stream Interception</h2>
            <p>Your media activities are private to your device. When you analyze a stream manifest or download video chunks, the software communicates directly between your local IP address and the remote content delivery network hosting the file. SaveZonix servers do <strong>NOT</strong> intercept, mirror, or log:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>The URLs, video links, or playlist manifests you submit;</li>
                <li>The video titles, creator names, or metadata parsed;</li>
                <li>The media files, video streams, or audio tracks downloaded onto your storage drive.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>2. Information We Collect (Minimal Essential Data Only)</h2>
            <p>If you create an optional user account, we store only the minimal technical data necessary to provide authentication and maintain your quota:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account Credentials:</strong> Full name, email address, salted password hash (via ASP.NET Core Identity PBKDF2 cryptography), and account creation timestamp. Plaintext passwords are never saved.</li>
                <li><strong>Personal Download History (User-Controlled):</strong> For registered users, download history records (video title, URL, size, timestamp) are stored in your personal database profile so you can manage your files. You can delete individual items or purge your entire history at any time.</li>
                <li><strong>Session &amp; Security Cookies:</strong> Secure, HTTP-only authentication tokens used exclusively for CSRF protection and login state management.</li>
                <li><strong>Guest Daily Quota:</strong> For unregistered guest users, daily usage counts are stored exclusively in your browser's local <code>localStorage</code> to maintain the fair daily limit.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. Information We Absolutely Do NOT Collect</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Zero Device Fingerprinting:</strong> We do not capture MAC addresses, hardware serial numbers, IMEI codes, or Canvas/WebGL device fingerprints.</li>
                <li><strong>Zero General Browsing Surveillance:</strong> The SaveZonix browser extension activates network inspection exclusively on pages where video manifests (HLS/DASH) are present. It never monitors, intercepts, or logs unrelated web browsing.</li>
                <li><strong>Zero Third-Party Marketing Trackers:</strong> We deploy no Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, or third-party behavioral tracking SDKs.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. User Rights (GDPR &amp; CCPA Compliance)</h2>
            <p>Under international privacy regulations (including GDPR and CCPA), you possess the following rights:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Right to Erasure (Right to be Forgotten):</strong> You may permanently delete your account and all associated download logs directly from your account portal or by emailing <a href="mailto:savezonix@gmail.com" class="auth-link">savezonix@gmail.com</a>.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> You can update your profile details and credentials at any time in your profile settings.</li>
                <li><strong>Right to Data Portability:</strong> You may export your personal download history upon request.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>5. Data Security</h2>
            <p>All network communications between your browser, desktop engine, and authentication endpoints utilize industry-standard TLS 1.3 encryption. Passwords and session keys are protected with salted cryptographic hashing.</p>

            <h2>6. Contact the Privacy Team</h2>
            <p>For inquiries regarding our privacy standards or data protection compliance, contact our privacy desk at <a href="mailto:savezonix@gmail.com" class="auth-link">savezonix@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
